1
00:00:09,400 --> 00:00:11,120
Try lightening up and stepping back,
will you?

2
00:00:20,180 --> 00:00:24,280
Anyone without money, come to my place.

3
00:00:24,280 --> 00:00:28,980
I don't have any either, but don't worry.

4
00:00:28,980 --> 00:00:32,800
Look at the blue sky.

5
00:00:33,700 --> 00:00:36,300
White clouds.

6
00:00:37,720 --> 00:00:42,740
Things will work out somehow, eventually.

7
00:00:55,880 --> 00:00:59,920
Anyone without a job, come to my place.

8
00:00:59,920 --> 00:01:04,560
I don't have any either, but don't worry.

9
00:01:06,300 --> 00:01:08,420
It's burning.

10
00:01:09,880 --> 00:01:12,120
Even the steel swarm.

11
00:01:13,440 --> 00:01:18,260
Things will work out somehow, eventually.

12
00:01:20,280 --> 00:01:21,540
You get it, right?

13
00:01:21,540 --> 00:01:23,520
I know, I know.

14
00:01:23,520 --> 00:01:27,460
Once you understand, shut up and follow me.

15
00:01:42,120 --> 00:01:44,900
A trolleybus! How nostalgic.

16
00:01:46,120 --> 00:01:47,660
What's a trolleybus?

17
00:01:47,660 --> 00:01:50,560
Officially, it's called a trolley bus.

18
00:01:50,560 --> 00:01:52,720
It's a car that runs on electricity.

19
00:01:52,720 --> 00:01:53,720
Electricity?

20
00:01:53,720 --> 00:01:55,620
See the poles up here?

21
00:01:55,620 --> 00:01:58,560
That's how it draws power
from the overhead wire to run.

22
00:01:59,100 --> 00:02:01,980
They look like insect antennae.
They're kind of cute.

23
00:02:02,380 --> 00:02:04,260
So it's a streetcar-type bus?

24
00:02:05,340 --> 00:02:06,260
Not quite.

25
00:02:06,260 --> 00:02:10,120
Streetcars draw power from both
the overhead wire and the rails,

26
00:02:10,120 --> 00:02:13,780
but this one only draws
power from its two poles.

27
00:02:14,600 --> 00:02:17,400
Since there's no need to lay tracks,
it's cheaper too,

28
00:02:17,400 --> 00:02:21,080
and back then it was what people now call an eco-friendly car,
you know.

29
00:02:22,520 --> 00:02:25,900
Actually,
I've driven a trolleybus myself, you know.

30
00:02:25,900 --> 00:02:26,680
Really?

31
00:02:27,020 --> 00:02:29,080
What do you mean? Tell us about it.

32
00:02:30,200 --> 00:02:33,260
It was back when I was
still in elementary school.

33
00:02:45,840 --> 00:02:50,900
Back in the day, Tokyo's skies were literally
crisscrossed with power lines everywhere you looked.

34
00:02:51,680 --> 00:02:57,180
In those days, the commoners' transport meant trains,
buses, streetcars, and trolleybuses.

35
00:02:57,800 --> 00:03:03,780
Streetcars could carry lots of people at once and were convenient,
but laying tracks was expensive.

36
00:03:04,260 --> 00:03:09,440
That's why trolleybuses, which need only overhead
wires and cost less than a third as much, drew attention.

37
00:03:11,880 --> 00:03:13,480
This is the prime seat, isn't it?

38
00:03:13,480 --> 00:03:14,520
Just an item.

39
00:03:15,760 --> 00:03:17,520
Was that the station where it stopped?

40
00:03:17,520 --> 00:03:19,800
No, the pole came off the overhead wire.

41
00:03:24,300 --> 00:03:26,400
You two are riding without paying

42
00:03:26,400 --> 00:03:28,940
No, we've got our fare, see?

43
00:03:28,940 --> 00:03:30,020
That's not the fare.

44
00:03:30,020 --> 00:03:33,040
If you're going to ride,
pay the proper fare.

45
00:03:34,260 --> 00:03:35,360
What if you get hurt?

46
00:03:35,360 --> 00:03:36,240
We're fine!

47
00:03:36,240 --> 00:03:38,560
Besides, let us help you fix it.

48
00:03:38,560 --> 00:03:40,360
Hey, it's dangerous. Get down!

49
00:03:40,360 --> 00:03:42,940
There's 600 volts of
current running through it!

50
00:03:42,940 --> 00:03:44,160
No worries, no worries.

51
00:03:44,160 --> 00:03:47,260
We're used to climbing 20,000-volt transmission towers,
you know.

52
00:03:47,680 --> 00:03:48,840
600 volts is nothing.

53
00:03:48,840 --> 00:03:52,380
You idiot, even 600 volts is
serious if you get electrocuted!

54
00:03:55,060 --> 00:03:56,300
I told you it's dangerous.

55
00:03:56,300 --> 00:03:59,580
You two really have no fear, do you?

56
00:04:00,760 --> 00:04:03,020
That driver was called Ken, you know.

57
00:04:04,260 --> 00:04:06,600
He had a quick temper,
always quick with his hands,

58
00:04:06,600 --> 00:04:08,700
and he was popular with the kids.

59
00:04:11,260 --> 00:04:13,200
Isn't that pole likely to come off?

60
00:04:13,400 --> 00:04:15,280
There's a lot of road
construction around here,

61
00:04:15,280 --> 00:04:17,540
and the shoes on the trolley
have worn down quite a bit.

62
00:04:17,540 --> 00:04:19,400
It's about time to replace them.

63
00:04:20,540 --> 00:04:21,320
There, that should do it.

64
00:04:22,600 --> 00:04:23,640
Sorry to keep you waiting.

65
00:04:24,240 --> 00:04:24,660
Here you go.

66
00:04:24,660 --> 00:04:25,580
There you go.

67
00:04:25,580 --> 00:04:26,360
Phew.

68
00:04:33,320 --> 00:04:34,540
It really does sway, doesn't it?

69
00:04:34,540 --> 00:04:37,620
All of Tokyo is covered
in Olympic construction.

70
00:04:37,620 --> 00:04:40,720
I hear there's even a plan
to build an expressway.

71
00:04:42,940 --> 00:04:43,820
That's good.

72
00:04:57,340 --> 00:04:58,560
It's you two again.

73
00:04:58,560 --> 00:04:59,880
Sorry.

74
00:05:03,820 --> 00:05:04,180
Thank you very much.

75
00:05:05,960 --> 00:05:07,340
What's wrong, Granny?

76
00:05:08,160 --> 00:05:10,840
That's strange, I can't find my wallet.

77
00:05:10,840 --> 00:05:12,960
It was right here a little while ago.

78
00:05:13,360 --> 00:05:14,680
It must have been then.

79
00:05:14,680 --> 00:05:16,680
When Kankichi scattered those marbles.

80
00:05:17,420 --> 00:05:19,560
Yeah, I must have lost it in the commotion.

81
00:05:20,420 --> 00:05:21,700
Alright, let's search!

82
00:05:21,700 --> 00:05:23,560
Hey, you two, help us look.

83
00:05:23,560 --> 00:05:23,840
Yeah.

84
00:05:24,680 --> 00:05:25,700
Sorry about this.

85
00:05:26,360 --> 00:05:27,640
Ma'am, what kind of wallet is it?

86
00:05:27,640 --> 00:05:29,220
It's a Hebikawa gamaguchi purse.

87
00:05:29,220 --> 00:05:32,740
A Hebikawa gamaguchi, Hebikawa, Hebikawa...

88
00:05:33,360 --> 00:05:34,280
I found it!

89
00:05:34,820 --> 00:05:37,650
This isn't the Hebikawa wallet,

90
00:05:37,700 --> 00:05:38,960
it's a snake toy.

91
00:05:38,960 --> 00:05:40,940
Damn it, where did it go?

92
00:05:42,200 --> 00:05:43,580
Wallet, wallet.

93
00:05:44,560 --> 00:05:46,000
It's right here.

94
00:05:47,860 --> 00:05:48,940
This one, right?

95
00:05:49,340 --> 00:05:52,680
Yes, that's it.
Phew, you saved me. Thank you.

96
00:05:52,680 --> 00:05:54,100
You're welcome.

97
00:05:54,780 --> 00:05:56,620
I thank you too, young man.

98
00:06:02,760 --> 00:06:04,260
See you, kids!

99
00:06:04,260 --> 00:06:08,000
Hey, next time take this
bus to your elementary school.

100
00:06:09,440 --> 00:06:12,280
Sure, I'll go anywhere there's a river.

101
00:06:12,280 --> 00:06:13,120
See ya.

102
00:06:14,540 --> 00:06:15,280
Goodbye.

103
00:06:16,920 --> 00:06:19,300
This loop at the terminal is impressive,
isn't it?

104
00:06:19,300 --> 00:06:21,580
But if you think about it, something's off.

105
00:06:22,200 --> 00:06:25,380
The U-turn makes the positive
and negative rotate, right?

106
00:06:25,740 --> 00:06:27,840
No matter how you think about it,
this'll short-circuit!

107
00:06:28,680 --> 00:06:30,820
You have to insulate the inside of the loop.

108
00:06:31,920 --> 00:06:32,600
Look.

109
00:06:32,600 --> 00:06:34,940
The positive and negative...

110
00:06:34,940 --> 00:06:36,120
They switched places.

111
00:06:36,720 --> 00:06:40,000
At the same time, it's converting
the vehicle motor and the poles.

112
00:06:40,520 --> 00:06:41,740
I don't get it at all.

113
00:06:41,740 --> 00:06:43,860
Chinkichi's a railway nut, you know.

114
00:06:44,800 --> 00:06:46,600
That's right,
Chinkichi could probably do it.

115
00:06:47,740 --> 00:06:51,380
We're going to run the trolleybus overhead
wires all the way to the front of the school.

116
00:06:53,040 --> 00:06:54,720
Did you really string up the wires?

117
00:06:54,720 --> 00:06:58,140
Of course,
when I say I'll do something, I do it.

118
00:06:59,260 --> 00:07:02,800
We hauled utility poles we didn't need anymore
from the scrapyard in the middle of the night,

119
00:07:03,320 --> 00:07:05,900
dug holes in front of the
school gate all night long,

120
00:07:05,900 --> 00:07:10,920
and by the time we were about to string the live wires and just needed to send the current through,
morning came.

121
00:07:11,480 --> 00:07:14,880
A teacher caught us,
and it was all torn down right away.

122
00:07:17,680 --> 00:07:19,520
The grown-ups were furious,

123
00:07:19,520 --> 00:07:21,760
but Ken just smiled.

124
00:07:24,180 --> 00:07:25,580
That's how it went one day.

125
00:07:29,200 --> 00:07:29,980
Ken-san,

126
00:07:29,980 --> 00:07:31,260
is your place near here?

127
00:07:32,180 --> 00:07:33,780
I have a bath at home too,

128
00:07:33,780 --> 00:07:35,600
but the big one's more relaxing.

129
00:07:36,160 --> 00:07:38,600
My house is near the trolleybus depot.

130
00:07:43,740 --> 00:07:45,200
So you got here first.

131
00:07:45,540 --> 00:07:46,380
You did it again

132
00:07:48,380 --> 00:07:49,740
This is Ken's

133
00:07:49,740 --> 00:07:51,780
My wife, Chieko.

134
00:07:52,320 --> 00:07:52,960
Nice to meet you.

135
00:07:52,960 --> 00:07:56,600
Y-yes, I'm Kankichi Ryotsu.

136
00:07:58,080 --> 00:08:02,060
I love trolleybuses, so I became a
driver despite my parents' objections.

137
00:08:02,060 --> 00:08:04,320
Once he makes up his mind,
he won't listen to anyone.

138
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:09,420
They opposed our marriage,
but I pushed through anyway.

139
00:08:12,480 --> 00:08:14,460
We're going to have a baby soon.

140
00:08:14,820 --> 00:08:17,520
He's already so restless and fidgety.

141
00:08:17,520 --> 00:08:20,180
I keep saying it's
definitely going to be a boy.

142
00:08:20,180 --> 00:08:23,460
You can't know that.
It might be a lively little girl.

143
00:08:23,460 --> 00:08:26,380
If it's a girl, it's better she
doesn't take after Ken, right?

144
00:08:26,380 --> 00:08:27,640
Hey, what did you just say?

145
00:08:29,340 --> 00:08:32,540
Well, boy or girl,
as long as it's healthy, either's fine.

146
00:08:33,140 --> 00:08:34,300
I'm sure it'll be fine.

147
00:08:34,960 --> 00:08:37,620
It moves around healthily
in my belly every day.

148
00:08:38,220 --> 00:08:41,560
After that, I quickly became
friends with Ken and the others.

149
00:08:44,920 --> 00:08:45,120
Yeah.

150
00:08:47,240 --> 00:08:48,420
Hey, Kankishi!

151
00:08:49,100 --> 00:08:50,260
Ken-saaan!

152
00:08:52,080 --> 00:08:53,740
Here I come, Ken-saaan!

153
00:08:53,740 --> 00:08:55,400
Come on, Kankishi!

154
00:08:55,400 --> 00:08:57,360
If you can hit it, go ahead and try!

155
00:08:58,560 --> 00:08:59,560
Got it!

156
00:09:03,320 --> 00:09:05,083
Don't get serious with kids like that,

157
00:09:05,133 --> 00:09:07,400
what are we supposed to
do if the ball gets lost?

158
00:09:08,040 --> 00:09:09,149
Sorry, sorry,

159
00:09:09,199 --> 00:09:12,180
if we can't find it, we'll pay for the ball.

160
00:09:14,460 --> 00:09:20,040
Ken loved baseball, loved children,
and above all, adored trolleybuses.

161
00:09:22,140 --> 00:09:25,460
This is the auxiliary engine switch,
and that's the regenerative current system.

162
00:09:25,460 --> 00:09:29,520
But trolleybuses like these were in an era
when ordinary people started owning cars.

163
00:09:29,520 --> 00:09:34,580
Pushed aside by the so-called car boom,
they gradually disappeared.

164
00:09:35,880 --> 00:09:36,540
What?!

165
00:09:37,360 --> 00:09:40,340
Amano-san and Miyata-san are being fired too,
because of the staff cuts?

166
00:09:42,180 --> 00:09:50,640
How could that be? Both of them have contributed the most to the company!
The company doesn't go by that kind of thing, and they're both getting on in years.

167
00:09:50,640 --> 00:09:59,160
That president will keep cutting heads one after another.
Screw that! Alright, I'll go negotiate with the president myself.

168
00:09:59,540 --> 00:10:01,820
Good, go give him a piece of your mind.

169
00:10:03,600 --> 00:10:09,540
President, even after I begged you this much, it's no good?
Nope, no way.

170
00:10:14,060 --> 00:10:17,780
Trolleybuses are outdated vehicles anyway.

171
00:10:17,780 --> 00:10:19,640
The era of private cars is here now.

172
00:10:19,640 --> 00:10:23,080
From now on,
our company won't be about trolleybuses.

173
00:10:23,080 --> 00:10:26,640
We're going to jump into new
businesses one after another.

174
00:10:26,640 --> 00:10:28,940
That's where the money is.

175
00:10:28,940 --> 00:10:33,840
What about Mr. Amano and Mr. Miyata?

176
00:10:33,840 --> 00:10:36,100
Firing them out of nowhere is too cruel!

177
00:10:36,940 --> 00:10:39,320
They're too old to find other work.

178
00:10:39,320 --> 00:10:43,000
Trolleybuses and those guys,
old things just have to quietly fade away.

179
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:44,040
That's just how the world is.

180
00:10:44,880 --> 00:10:48,260
Once you understand, get back to work.

181
00:10:49,260 --> 00:10:50,280
What do you think you're doing?

182
00:10:51,040 --> 00:10:52,060
Hey, you!

183
00:10:52,060 --> 00:10:52,800
What?

184
00:10:52,800 --> 00:10:53,820
I'm the president.

185
00:11:03,500 --> 00:11:05,000
God, god, god!

186
00:11:06,960 --> 00:11:08,380
Call the police!

187
00:11:09,320 --> 00:11:11,280
Ryo-san!

188
00:11:13,500 --> 00:11:14,580
Let's go, Gacchi!

189
00:11:15,000 --> 00:11:15,620
Yeah!

190
00:11:24,120 --> 00:11:27,440
Yay! I went just as fast as Ken-san!

191
00:11:28,220 --> 00:11:29,260
Not again...

192
00:11:36,220 --> 00:11:37,300
Ken-san

193
00:11:37,300 --> 00:11:38,540
What?

194
00:11:39,180 --> 00:11:40,600
It must be some kind of mistake.

195
00:11:40,600 --> 00:11:42,160
No way, it's definitely Ken-san.

196
00:11:42,160 --> 00:11:43,740
Let's go check.

197
00:11:43,740 --> 00:11:44,440
Yeah.

198
00:11:44,860 --> 00:11:46,280
Alright, let's go see.

199
00:11:46,280 --> 00:11:46,700
Hey.

200
00:11:51,760 --> 00:11:53,380
Are you absolutely sure about that?

201
00:11:53,380 --> 00:11:56,440
Apparently he got cut and
then went and threw a punch.

202
00:11:56,440 --> 00:11:58,280
Ken does have a short temper, after all.

203
00:11:59,260 --> 00:12:00,840
Mister, can't you do something about this?

204
00:12:00,840 --> 00:12:01,800
That's right.

205
00:12:01,800 --> 00:12:03,500
Poor Ken.

206
00:12:03,500 --> 00:12:05,140
Even if you say that,

207
00:12:05,600 --> 00:12:06,080
I see.

208
00:12:06,780 --> 00:12:07,140
Right.

209
00:12:07,540 --> 00:12:08,480
Where's the president?

210
00:12:08,480 --> 00:12:11,820
If it's the president,
he went home in a rage.

211
00:12:12,420 --> 00:12:14,120
Alright, let's go help Ken.

212
00:12:14,120 --> 00:12:15,960
We'll go to the president's
house and confront him directly.

213
00:12:15,960 --> 00:12:17,120
Follow me!

214
00:12:29,740 --> 00:12:33,220
What? Cancel Ken's dismissal, he says?

215
00:12:33,500 --> 00:12:36,260
Ken's about to have a baby.

216
00:12:36,600 --> 00:12:38,620
Firing him now is so cruel.

217
00:12:38,980 --> 00:12:41,300
Well, that's none of my business.

218
00:12:41,680 --> 00:12:44,220
I said no means no. Go home, go home!

219
00:12:44,220 --> 00:12:48,780
Ken went to protest on behalf of the trolleybus drivers,
didn't he?

220
00:12:48,780 --> 00:12:52,120
It's not right to pin
all the blame on Ken alone.

221
00:12:52,480 --> 00:12:53,120
That's right, that's right!

222
00:12:53,620 --> 00:12:55,240
No matter what you say, it's a no.

223
00:12:55,240 --> 00:12:57,980
Anyway, trolleybuses aren't needed anymore.

224
00:13:00,580 --> 00:13:01,220
Why?

225
00:13:01,220 --> 00:13:04,060
Sales keep dropping and
we're just piling up losses.

226
00:13:04,060 --> 00:13:08,060
Vehicle upkeep costs money, and on top of that,
they spoil the city's scenery.

227
00:13:08,060 --> 00:13:10,080
What's wrong with having trolleybus lines?

228
00:13:10,080 --> 00:13:11,500
They're cool, damn it!

229
00:13:11,500 --> 00:13:16,160
Shut up! Either way, we don't need
outdated junk like that anymore.

230
00:13:16,160 --> 00:13:17,360
That's just cruel.

231
00:13:17,360 --> 00:13:19,400
We ride them every day, you know.

232
00:13:19,400 --> 00:13:23,080
What do noisy kids know about business?

233
00:13:23,580 --> 00:13:24,480
Get out, you brats!

234
00:13:25,900 --> 00:13:27,340
Come on, get going!

235
00:13:27,340 --> 00:13:29,300
If you don't leave, I'll call the police!

236
00:13:29,620 --> 00:13:30,360
Damn it!

237
00:13:31,280 --> 00:13:32,300
You stubborn old fool!

238
00:13:37,620 --> 00:13:39,280
Ugh, what a nasty guy.

239
00:13:39,280 --> 00:13:42,560
No matter how rich he is, I don't want to
grow up to be a man like that, you know?

240
00:13:49,320 --> 00:13:50,240
Damn it!

241
00:13:52,320 --> 00:13:53,600
I wonder what happened to Ken.

242
00:13:54,480 --> 00:13:56,120
I wonder if he still hasn't come
back from the police station.

243
00:14:15,420 --> 00:14:18,240
Kankichi-kun.

244
00:14:18,620 --> 00:14:20,580
Ken hasn't come home yet?

245
00:14:21,060 --> 00:14:21,720
That's right.

246
00:14:22,440 --> 00:14:23,840
Anyway, come inside.

247
00:14:34,540 --> 00:14:37,420
I understand how you feel,
but hitting him would be bad.

248
00:14:37,420 --> 00:14:39,920
It'll only make our
side's argument fall apart.

249
00:14:40,640 --> 00:14:43,540
I know,
but I got laid off and it just happened.

250
00:14:44,240 --> 00:14:47,380
Well, I have a few leads on new jobs myself.

251
00:14:47,380 --> 00:14:50,660
With a baby on the way,
we can't just sit around.

252
00:14:51,060 --> 00:14:51,760
Sorry.

253
00:14:51,760 --> 00:14:54,880
Excuse me, detective, can't I go home now?

254
00:14:55,040 --> 00:14:56,840
My wife is all alone at home.

255
00:14:57,340 --> 00:14:59,900
Go home? The cars and trains aren't running.

256
00:14:59,900 --> 00:15:01,340
Then run home.

257
00:15:01,340 --> 00:15:02,640
Don't be ridiculous.

258
00:15:03,440 --> 00:15:05,460
Well, right now is the worst it's been.

259
00:15:05,460 --> 00:15:06,940
Wait a little longer.

260
00:15:06,940 --> 00:15:09,200
The storm will calm down before long.

261
00:15:19,480 --> 00:15:21,520
What a terrible storm it's turned into.

262
00:15:22,480 --> 00:15:24,960
Stay here until it dies down a bit more.

263
00:15:27,040 --> 00:15:29,700
I wonder what's happened to my husband.

264
00:15:30,120 --> 00:15:32,900
Knowing Ken, he's probably already
off fiddling with the car's ride height

265
00:15:34,420 --> 00:15:35,140
What do you mean?

266
00:15:37,060 --> 00:15:39,440
It's not that I was keeping it a secret,

267
00:15:40,500 --> 00:15:41,380
what happened?

268
00:15:45,960 --> 00:15:48,080
It's all that idiot president's fault.

269
00:15:49,200 --> 00:15:50,020
So that's how it is.

270
00:15:52,120 --> 00:15:54,740
Thank you all so much for worrying about us.

271
00:15:55,560 --> 00:15:57,060
We'll be fine.

272
00:15:57,060 --> 00:16:00,880
Even if he's lost his job,
the baby's still going to be born.

273
00:16:00,880 --> 00:16:02,960
There's no point in fretting over it.

274
00:16:03,340 --> 00:16:05,140
What a hopeless father he is.

275
00:16:05,820 --> 00:16:07,080
Forget about that guy

276
00:16:07,080 --> 00:16:09,500
Shall we all go get something good to eat?

277
00:16:12,620 --> 00:16:14,000
What's wrong, ma'am?

278
00:16:15,900 --> 00:16:16,720
The baby's

279
00:16:17,120 --> 00:16:18,720
The baby's about to be born!

280
00:16:20,140 --> 00:16:21,040
This is bad!

281
00:16:21,660 --> 00:16:23,400
We have to call an ambulance!

282
00:16:24,160 --> 00:16:24,940
The phone...

283
00:16:24,940 --> 00:16:27,980
There's no phone! We have to go get one.

284
00:16:30,900 --> 00:16:31,620
The water...

285
00:16:32,960 --> 00:16:36,460
is flooding the road. We can't go like this,
and an ambulance can't get through either.

286
00:16:37,040 --> 00:16:38,520
What do we do, Kankichi?

287
00:16:41,460 --> 00:16:44,540
That's it!
We'll carry her to the hospital with that.

288
00:16:47,920 --> 00:16:53,980
Okay, overhead wire, voltmeter, ammeter, all set!
As expected of a district full of railfans, Kankichi.

289
00:16:53,980 --> 00:17:00,840
Hurry up! Alright, let's go!
Okay, trolleybus, roll out!

290
00:17:13,420 --> 00:17:14,280
I wish you could've seen that.

291
00:17:25,760 --> 00:17:27,780
Man, those kids from earlier

292
00:17:27,780 --> 00:17:28,740
really wore us out

293
00:17:29,280 --> 00:17:31,240
Those brats were so cheeky.

294
00:17:31,680 --> 00:17:33,500
Honestly, sticking their noses

295
00:17:33,500 --> 00:17:34,660
into the adult world like that

296
00:17:34,660 --> 00:17:35,800
is completely out of line.

297
00:17:36,560 --> 00:17:39,280
That's right. Kids should just stick
to having babies one after another.

298
00:17:44,760 --> 00:17:48,100
What now, Kankichi? There are no overhead
wires all the way to the hospital.

299
00:17:48,540 --> 00:17:52,080
Leave it to me. Power ends here.
Lower the trolley poles.

300
00:17:53,380 --> 00:17:57,100
This one has the latest
auxiliary diesel engine.

301
00:17:57,380 --> 00:17:58,220
I see.

302
00:18:03,800 --> 00:18:05,060
Trolley pole stowed.

303
00:18:05,640 --> 00:18:06,480
Right, switch places.

304
00:18:11,900 --> 00:18:14,400
It's reversing.
Just as expected from the latest model.

305
00:18:15,340 --> 00:18:17,620
Kankichi, hurry up or

306
00:18:17,620 --> 00:18:18,520
Got it.

307
00:18:25,000 --> 00:18:27,900
If it weren't for that idiot president's house,
this would be a shortcut.

308
00:18:27,900 --> 00:18:29,680
We don't have time to go around.

309
00:18:29,680 --> 00:18:32,140
We'll have to cut
through the garden somehow.

310
00:18:32,620 --> 00:18:35,520
A baby matters more than
the president's house.

311
00:18:40,840 --> 00:18:43,600
From now on,
it's the age of real estate sales.

312
00:18:44,480 --> 00:18:46,020
What's that?

313
00:18:49,900 --> 00:18:52,020
Please drive more safely.

314
00:18:52,020 --> 00:18:52,960
I know.

315
00:19:26,980 --> 00:19:28,800
What on earth happened?

316
00:19:35,020 --> 00:19:36,460
Are you all right, ma'am?

317
00:19:52,000 --> 00:19:53,960
Hello, this is Asakusa Police Station.

318
00:19:54,760 --> 00:19:58,540
What? A kid took the trolleybus and
crashed into President Akashima's house?

319
00:19:59,280 --> 00:19:59,920
What?!

320
00:20:09,340 --> 00:20:10,520
Hey! Kankichi!

321
00:20:12,060 --> 00:20:12,700
Ken-san!

322
00:20:15,920 --> 00:20:17,480
Are you guys okay?

323
00:20:18,720 --> 00:20:22,680
Ken-san, the baby's coming, so we...

324
00:20:22,680 --> 00:20:23,880
What? Really?

325
00:20:24,960 --> 00:20:25,680
It's coming!

326
00:20:29,080 --> 00:20:30,000
It's here!

327
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:31,700
Congratulations, Ken-san!

328
00:20:31,820 --> 00:20:32,380
Yay!

329
00:20:32,540 --> 00:20:33,560
Ken-san, you're a dad!

330
00:20:41,440 --> 00:20:42,600
Congratulations!

331
00:20:43,600 --> 00:20:45,320
Yes, it's a healthy baby boy.

332
00:20:47,700 --> 00:20:50,180
A boy, well done, Chieko.

333
00:20:50,740 --> 00:20:53,500
It was close. Another minute later
and it would have been dangerous.

334
00:20:54,960 --> 00:20:55,400
Thanks to you all.

335
00:20:56,980 --> 00:20:59,320
In that case, it couldn't be helped.

336
00:21:01,280 --> 00:21:02,220
We did it!

337
00:21:05,980 --> 00:21:07,820
He looks just like Ken.

338
00:21:12,400 --> 00:21:17,060
Even in an emergency,
driving a trolleybus into a house!

339
00:21:17,060 --> 00:21:19,040
That must have been a real
ordeal afterward, right?

340
00:21:19,040 --> 00:21:22,980
Yeah, we got a huge scolding from the old man and the teacher,
of course.

341
00:21:24,960 --> 00:21:27,440
Everyone in town took
our side when we rode it.

342
00:21:28,640 --> 00:21:35,140
Ahhhh, that president cashed in a
fortune on insurance and rebuilt his house.

343
00:21:35,140 --> 00:21:37,380
That's what they say, anyway.

344
00:21:38,360 --> 00:21:43,720
Thinking about it now, trolleybuses were
actually eco-friendly vehicles, weren't they?

345
00:21:43,720 --> 00:21:50,160
They're quiet and don't give off exhaust fumes.
I feel like they're exactly the kind of vehicle we need today.

346
00:21:50,160 --> 00:21:56,060
Yeah, but back then it was different.
Private cars and taxis kept multiplying.

347
00:21:56,060 --> 00:21:59,180
Hardly anyone rode the trolleybuses anymore.

348
00:22:00,260 --> 00:22:05,800
Road congestion grew worse by the day, and
trolleybuses were no longer the people's transport,

349
00:22:05,800 --> 00:22:11,800
but a slow, obstructive presence.
Trolleybuses were pushed off the roads

350
00:22:12,160 --> 00:22:18,360
and abolished one after another. Today's the last day.
I wish we could keep them running longer.

351
00:22:20,160 --> 00:22:22,980
We came too? Kin-san!

352
00:22:23,260 --> 00:22:24,700
So you came after all?

353
00:22:24,860 --> 00:22:28,240
Yeah, we have to see its final ride off.

354
00:22:43,860 --> 00:22:47,880
That's the Type 50, number 77,
the one Kin-san used to drive!

355
00:22:50,320 --> 00:22:52,260
But the trolley shoes are worn down.

356
00:22:55,380 --> 00:22:57,460
They don't need to replace them anymore,
do they.

357
00:22:59,020 --> 00:22:59,860
Never again.

358
00:23:01,540 --> 00:23:05,100
Ken-san's face back then looked so lonely.

359
00:23:10,820 --> 00:23:14,400
Sure, the world has become
richer compared to those days,

360
00:23:14,400 --> 00:23:17,520
but somehow I wonder if
that was really a good thing.

361
00:23:17,520 --> 00:23:18,700
Exactly.

362
00:23:20,520 --> 00:23:22,940
Ryotsu, you actually say
something smart once in a while.

363
00:23:23,820 --> 00:23:28,000
People have lost many good things
in exchange for their prosperity.

364
00:23:28,720 --> 00:23:30,520
We tend to forget, though.

365
00:23:31,000 --> 00:23:33,400
Chief, I'll never forget!

366
00:23:33,400 --> 00:23:36,980
In your case, it's not that you don't forget,
it's that you don't progress.

367
00:23:38,000 --> 00:23:41,080
You haven't gotten richer,
and your head is still as poor as ever.

368
00:23:41,880 --> 00:23:45,280
You're still the same kid
who drove that trolleybus

369
00:23:46,180 --> 00:23:48,320
Listen, you lot, don't you start making me

370
00:23:50,260 --> 00:23:53,660
Well, people don't need to
force themselves to change, right?

371
00:23:53,660 --> 00:23:56,980
No, in your case,
you'd better change a little.

372
00:23:56,980 --> 00:23:57,540
Urk!

373
00:23:58,060 --> 00:24:00,360
No way! Chief!

374
00:24:46,480 --> 00:24:49,920
Thanks for watching.

375
00:24:50,160 --> 00:24:53,460
We were kids once, but everyone's forgotten.

376
00:24:54,580 --> 00:24:57,640
Politicians with their self-important faces,

377
00:24:57,640 --> 00:25:00,900
and blue-eyeshadowed aunties too.

378
00:25:00,900 --> 00:25:03,920
Come on, turn the corner.

379
00:25:04,500 --> 00:25:06,500
That corner there.

380
00:25:07,560 --> 00:25:11,700
You'll get to meet everyone, everyone.

381
00:25:12,280 --> 00:25:16,320
Over there, it's Kame-ari.

382
00:25:17,600 --> 00:25:19,620
Surely, Kame-ari.

383
00:25:21,100 --> 00:25:24,920
Everyone, come to our town!

384
00:25:26,020 --> 00:25:26,460
Thank you.

385
00:25:30,640 --> 00:25:33,140
March 3rd is my birthday.

386
00:25:33,140 --> 00:25:35,260
But every year, on that very day,

387
00:25:35,260 --> 00:25:37,900
one disaster after another strikes me.

388
00:25:37,900 --> 00:25:40,080
I was sure this year would be different.

389
00:25:40,080 --> 00:25:43,300
Where on earth am I headed?

390
00:25:43,300 --> 00:25:47,240
Next time:
"Misery After Misery Birthday." See you then!

391
00:25:55,960 --> 00:25:56,440
Thank you.

